  "body": "## What changed\n- **Model:** `HeightReference::WorkOffset` names no slot any more. It resolves through `setup::wcs_slot(world, setup)` (the setup's pick, else G54). That is the same law the post uses, so an operation can't disagree with its setup. `posting::wcs_context` and `wcs_slot` no longer take the op's params. The #196 post refusal for \"height on another slot than the pick\" is removed because that state can't be built any more. The one-file shared-word refusal stays.\n- **Heights page:** the Work offset reference no longer has a WCS combo. It shows a read-only \"Work offset\" row, e.g. `G55 (setup Setup1 - set on the Setups page)`, with a hover hint.\n- **Setups page / setup sheet:** the unpicked entry was \"Auto (from heights, else G54)\" and is now \"G54 (default)\". The sheet now says `program offset: G54 (the default - not picked)`. The viewport plane chip shows the setup's G-word.\n- **Project v52 + migration** (`crates/app/src/project/wcs_migrate.rs`). It runs before any world write. For each setup it collects every slot in use: the pick, each op's v51 posted slot, and every height's slot (suppressed ops included).\n  - **One slot:** the slot moves onto the setup's `work_offset` (G54 stays unwritten). Stamps and posts don't change.\n  - **Several slots:** the load is refused by name (`ProjectError::WorkOffsetConflict`). The message lists each op with its slots, e.g. `setup Setup1: Face1 (G55); Face2 (G56)`.\n  - **No setup to hold the pick:** documents without setups load if everything is G54; any other slot is refused by name.\n  - **v52 files:** a height that carries a slot is refused as corrupt. The MCP params door refuses one too.\n- **Stamp:** a work-offset height feeds the resolved setup slot into the stamp. Migrated ops keep bit-identical stamps, so goldens don't change.\n- Why the load is refused rather than loaded with a post refusal is in `docs/decisions/329-setup-defines-wcs.md`. Loading would mean either keeping per-height slots in memory or re-pointing the op on its next regeneration.\n\n## Readings / tests (debug, worktree target)\n- New `crates/app/tests/setup_defines_wcs.rs` (4 tests):\n  - agreeing v51 file (per-height G55): the setup picks G55, the post is byte-identical and the resave equals the v52 save; a G54 file stays unpicked\n  - conflicting setup: refused by name (G55/G56, G55/G54, and a picked setup with another height slot)\n  - document without setups: refused by name\n  - v52 height carrying a slot: refused as corrupt\n- `setup_wcs::work_offset_heights_follow_the_setups_pick_and_its_undo`: picking G56 moves every work-offset height and stales the op; undo moves them back and redo moves them again. This replaces the removed #196 conflict test.\n- ui lib `egui_app::setup_wcs_tests::the_heights_page_shows_the_setups_offset_with_no_wcs_choice`: one combo only (From), and the row follows the setup's pick. Run from CWD `crates/ui`: 286 passed, 0 failed.\n- Green: setup_wcs, rotated_wcs, wcs_align, posting, project_roundtrip, commands_undo, conformance, golden_cl, fanuc_post, heights, heights_selection, setups, setup_sheet, lathe_spindle_law, lathe_post_refusals, heidenhain_block_form, mcp, operations, app lib, ui operations. No golden or snapshot changed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Not exercised: the GUI by hand, the release heavy lanes, and batch suites outside the list above.\n\nChangelog: A height measured from the work offset now reads its setup's offset (picked on the Setups page); the Heights page no longer offers a per-height WCS choice, and older projects migrate their slot onto the setup, or are refused by name when one setup's operations used different offsets (project v52) (#329)\n\nFixes #329\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: project files are now v52. A height referencing the work offset no longer stores its own G54-G59 slot - the setup defines it. Older builds refuse v52 files, and a v51-or-older project whose operations used different work-offset slots within one setup is refused at load by name (open it in an earlier release, make the slots agree, save, then open it here). Agreed by the maintainer 2026-11-08.\n",
